Package: BayesLinReg
Title: Bayesian Linear Regression with Flexible Coefficient Priors
Version: 14.5.0
Authors@R:
    person(
        "Fabio", "Morgante",
        email = "fabiom@clemson.edu",
        role = c("aut", "cre")
    )
Description: Fits Bayesian linear regression models from raw observations,
    genome-wide association study summary statistics with block-aware linkage
    disequilibrium matrices, or dense, sparse, or low-rank eigen sufficient
    statistics with one or more predictor blocks.
    Coefficients can be assigned unpenalized flat priors, independent normal,
    spike-and-slab, BayesR-style spike-and-multiple-slab, or beta-prime
    global-local priors, including
    Strawderman-Berger and
    horseshoe specifications. Supports known or inverse-gamma-modeled residual
    variance, expected-proportion-of-variance scale calibration, sampled
    coefficient-prior variances, optional posterior block and total variance
    explained, Gibbs sampling implemented in R or 'Rcpp', optional parallel
    chains, memory-efficient online posterior summaries, predictor
    standardization, optional within-chain parallel Gram-block and low-rank
    eigen-block updates,
    posterior summaries, credible and predictive intervals, and convergence
    diagnostics.
